{
  "_comment": [
    "Your hand-made verdicts. They always win over every automatic layer",
    "(tags, rules, Wikipedia/Wikidata/MusicBrainz, the LLM and the audio",
    "classifier), and they are never overwritten by a re-run.",
    "",
    "Three ways to use it:",
    "",
    "  1. Force the styles of one artist:",
    "       \"artists\": {",
    "         \"Withered Throne\": { \"styles\": [\"Melodic Death Metal\"], \"note\": \"tag says only 'Metal'\" }",
    "       }",
    "",
    "  1b. Lock that verdict so every automatic label is removed and only your",
    "      styles remain (use this when a tag or the LLM got the artist wrong):",
    "       \"artists\": {",
    "         \"Kadjo\": { \"styles\": [\"Deathcore\", \"Metalcore\"], \"exclusive\": true }",
    "       }",
    "",
    "  2. Force the styles of one album (keyed by 'artist :: album'):",
    "       \"albums\": {",
    "         \"Kamelot :: The Awakening\": { \"styles\": [\"Power Metal\", \"Symphonic Metal\"] }",
    "       }",
    "",
    "  3. Force (or clear) one single track (keyed by its path relative to the",
    "     music root):",
    "       \"tracks\": {",
    "         \"Accept - Humanoid (2024)/01. Humanoid.mp3\": { \"styles\": [\"Heavy Metal\"] }",
    "       }",
    "",
    "An empty style list means 'no style at all' - use it to push a track into",
    "the 'unlabelled' bucket so it is never picked by a style filter.",
    "",
    "Style names must match data/styles.json. Run step4_normalize.py again",
    "after editing this file; it re-applies the overrides to the whole library."
  ],
